  "body": "**Link to problem area**: https://spec.matrix.org/latest/client-server-api/#profiles\r\n\r\n**Issue**\r\n\r\nIt does not state how to remove a user's avatar. By inspecting Element's network requests, I can see that you have to set it to the empty string. \r\n\r\nThe docs for `PUT /_matrix/client/v3/profile/{userId}/avatar_url` do not state that `avatar_url` is a required parameter, so not specifying the key or setting it to null are plausible ways to remove it. If you do not specify the key, Synapse gives a `M_MISSING_PARAM`. If `null`, Synapse gives a `M_INVALID_PARAM`. Other homeserver implementations may do something different, since it is not specified what should happen.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, there is no `DELETE /_matrix/client/v3/profile/{userId}/avatar_url`. That would be the most intuitive to use, but would require modifying the spec and implementations rather than just a clarification.\r\n\r\n",
